<%# The footer lockup's styles (the `lockup:` fact; docs/SITE_FOOTER.md). Only
    a footer that declares a lockup renders this, so a footer without one is
    byte for byte what it was before the fact existed.

    HEIGHT-LED. The lockup is drawn at --ftr-lockup-height (default 7rem, about
    the icon-and-name block's height plus the room a stacked logo's second line
    needs) and its width follows the artwork, never wider than its column. The
    width and height attributes give the box its shape before the file loads.

    CENTRED. A lockup centres the brand block (.ftr-brand-lockup): the lockup,
    the tagline, the email and the social row. A stacked lockup is symmetric
    about its own centre, so it reads as the column's heading only when
    centred under it. The link columns keep their alignment. The home link is
    inline-flex, so it hugs the artwork (centred by the block's text-align)
    and its focus ring, offset 4px, rings the lockup instead of running
    across the column through the name.

    THEME SWAP. Light shows on a light page, dark under the root's `dark`
    class. The hide rule comes after the display rule, so it wins on order. %>
<style>
  .ftr-lockup { display: block; width: auto; height: var(--ftr-lockup-height, 7rem); max-width: 100%;
    object-fit: contain; object-position: center; }
  .ftr-brand-lockup { text-align: center; }
  .ftr-brand-lockup .ftr-home { display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; vertical-align: top; }
  .ftr-brand-lockup .ftr-home:focus-visible { outline-offset: 4px; }
  .ftr-brand-lockup .ftr-socials { justify-content: center; }
  .ftr-lockup-dark { display: none; }
  .dark .ftr-lockup-light { display: none; }
  .dark .ftr-lockup-dark { display: block; }
</style>
